								<td align="left" valign="middle"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3311.msg37301#msg37301"><img src="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/Themes/safgrey105/images/post/xx.gif" alt="" border="0" /></a></td>
								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3311.msg37301#msg37301">Re: University of Florida Student Tasered @ John Kerry Speech</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #19 on:</b> September 20, 2007, 12:46:12 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">also, i&#039;m not going to say that the kid deserved what he got, or that the police were right to do what they did.  but honestly, the kid could have avoided everything if he&#039;d have used his brains a little.  i think the police were 100% in the wrong to try to stop his questions and to arrest him, that they made up charges about insiting a riot show that even they knew that.  but once they told him to leave and he didn&#039;t, then told him he was under arrest, his trying to pull away and leave, got him grabbed, his continuing to try to pull away got him taken down, and his struggling and resistance to rolling over and getting handcuffed got him tazed.  its a pretty standard escalation of force to gain compliance.  and to be honest, i think the only reason they were repremanded by their chief for their conduct was that they did this all on national TV.  that being said i don&#039;t think its right that police can do this, i don&#039;t think its just or moral, but it is the way things are and is to be expected if you resist arrest.  so like i said before, i&#039;m not gonna say the kid got what was comming to him, nobody deserves that imo.  but he had to know it was comming.  thats at least part of why i think he planned this, at least in part, ahead of time, because he had to have known what he was provoking by struggling with officers.  from the questions he was asking and what i&#039;ve read about him i don&#039;t believe he&#039;s dumb enought not to know.  its speculative of course, but i smell deception.<br /></div>
						</td>
					</tr>
