							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;"><div class="quoteheader"><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3311.msg37304#msg37304">Quote from: Matt Jay on September 20, 2007, 12:54:05 pm</a></div><div class="quote">That makes sense Budaho.<br /><br />Although to me his struggling when they initially apprehended him seemed like a realistic reaction. He really literally did NOTHING to warrant being arrested up until that point when he started resisting. It wouldn&#039;t have made any sense if they grabbed him and he was just like &quot;damn&quot; and walked out with them.<br /></div><br />oh i totally agree.&nbsp; i mean my natural reaction if someone grabs me from behind and starts walking me out is to snap their arm and throw them to the ground.&nbsp; but around people who are authrorized to shoot and or beat you for not complying with their orders, natural and instinctive reactions are not always wize, even if they are understandable.&nbsp; cause trust me the police aren&#039;t going to take the realisticness of your resistance into account when they are clubbing / tazing you.&nbsp; he had every right to have been surprised at their arrest of him, and he had every right to protest the fact verbally.&nbsp; but using even just a tinny ammount of force against a police officer is dumb, and going to have bad consequences for you.&nbsp; if you&#039;re gonna resist, you damn well better put them down as hard and fast as you can, then get out damn quick&nbsp; cause more will be comming for you real quick.&nbsp; resisting half assed just enough to provoke an escalation doesn&#039;t make any sense.&nbsp; especially once the kid was on the ground with 4 of them telling him repeatedly that if he didn&#039;t stop struggling and roll over he was going to get tazed.&nbsp; what are you gonna do from that position, his continued struggling from this point on either makes him completely retarded, or trying to provoke a response.&nbsp; at least thats the only way i can figure it.</div>
