								<td align="left" valign="middle">
									<b><a href="http://masslinemedia.com/smf/index.php?topic=3311.msg37368#msg37368">Re: University of Florida Student Tasered @ John Kerry Speech</a></b>
									<div class="smalltext">&#171; <b>Reply #25 on:</b> September 21, 2007, 07:15:27 pm &#187;</div></td>
								<td align="right" valign="bottom" height="20" nowrap="nowrap" style="font-size: smaller;">
								</td>
							</tr></table>
							<hr width="100%" size="1" class="hrcolor" />
							<div style="overflow: auto; width: 100%;">I think it&#039;s funny that you use that picture, even though you hold against that kid for not using his head or using logic. If the Black Panthers used their heads, they wouldn&#039;t exist because Fred Hampton would know he would get a bullet in his head by the CIA. Yeah, the smart thing to do would not to resist because it&#039;s very obvious what is going to happen if you resist. <br /><br />I would agree with you if the power dynamic between this guy and this police was equal. The guy did no action but is held responsible for no action,yet the police did all the action and are not held responsible. <br /><br />I don&#039;t think that he was just resisting because he was surprised or because that&#039;s a natural reaction to getting grabbed (and it is a natural reaction to be surprised and react when you&#039;re grabbed but not when you&#039;re pretty fully aware that you&#039;re surrounded by cops). For the most part he reacted that way because he was scared shitless, this guy isn&#039;t down and out and has nothing left to lose, this guy is a white university student who is trying to look tight by trying to make a celebrity look bad. When the cops got hold of him he got scared and thought his mommy or daddy or some kind of similar figure to save him, in the same way that he has been rescued his whole life. <br /><br />I mean I ain&#039;t crying over that this guy got tazered, lots of more fucked up shit has happened, in the united states, all over the world, but its dangerous to think about it in that way,in a sort of ride the fence way.<br /><br />Not trying to diss or offend.<br /><br /><br /></div>
						</td>
